{"data":{"featured":{"edges":[{"node":{"frontmatter":{"title":"NetFlow","cover":{"publicURL":"/static/8dedd4f2de499286c3a5f9fe72c849f9/NetFlow_Topology.png"},"gif":{"publicURL":"/static/f5c8e2a7c7b4f54ec530bd9f9ad7ef4a/NetFlow.gif"},"gallery":[{"publicURL":"/static/b40a597b6012b030671f80f5ec2c6dc6/Netflow_Create_Bar.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/e3c01e9e3b8474aa81aa1753be3b1266/Device_Simple.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/1439a7a5fef39d512409201898ed2627/Connection_Established.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/e74045e28815df765adc737d4adf4854/SSID_Connections.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/00bccf9ebbf354cd4f6a93ff6778ab58/AP_Connections.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/547845944c8b81b6bec635d1c2958383/Server+Connections.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/0ec85220c035abd820695a3ae311b1ad/Switch_Profile.png"}],"tech":["React","JavaScript","Network Engineering","GitHub Pages","Network Visualization"],"github":"https://github.com/esixtosr/NetFlow","external":"https://esixtosr.github.io/NetFlow/network/home-lab/","cta":null,"featured":null},"html":"<p>NetFlow is an interactive network topology tool I built to design and document network layouts, VLAN segmentation, and infrastructure relationships.</p>\n<p>It lets users create devices, define connections, organize VLAN environments, and export diagrams for documentation, planning, and analysis.</p>"}},{"node":{"frontmatter":{"title":"Enterprise SIEM Lab","cover":{"publicURL":"/static/79ca89056ac964da68e787873cd11255/01-mitre-attack-dashboard.png"},"gif":null,"gallery":[{"publicURL":"/static/916c326d7414e08796f68ae8daf49da4/02-role-based-vpn-siem-architecture.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/2781a7439eb436f102bfebe2e3bf6424/03-active-directory-role-based-groups.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/61a97d12b5ba975785b78bdcf170be2f/04-wazuh-endpoint-agents.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/e155327557b4d539dfa4c8cd72c44419/05-failed-logon-detection-filter.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/2cdcd267335f3823d69434ad3778c3f7/06-failed-logon-event-details.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/7c2c6f5ebfb78c3dc8096493fa12b9ad/07-dc01-endpoint-posture.png"}],"tech":["Wazuh","Active Directory","VPN","MITRE ATT&CK","Windows Server","SIEM"],"github":null,"external":null,"cta":null,"featured":null},"html":"<p>An enterprise-style SIEM lab built to monitor VPN access, Active Directory groups, Windows endpoints, and security events through Wazuh.</p>\n<p>The lab maps user roles to network access, collects endpoint telemetry, and validates detections such as failed logons, authentication activity, and endpoint posture from a centralized dashboard.</p>"}},{"node":{"frontmatter":{"title":"12U Bare-Metal Homelab","cover":{"publicURL":"/static/8702f5859fc8a6b032e0c921eb389d86/Unifi_Dashboard.png"},"gif":null,"gallery":[{"publicURL":"/static/9422537eb3bf0071f6a2e210a9da8c58/Closed_Server_Rack.jpg"},{"publicURL":"/static/ba39f6f878837c361aaae1a93881eca2/Opened_Server_Rack.jpg"},{"publicURL":"/static/7d6cd119ca453bdf26a3c0f00f03ad7f/Port_Connections.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/8dedd4f2de499286c3a5f9fe72c849f9/NetFlow_Topology.png"}],"tech":["UniFi","Proxmox","VLANs","Network Engineering","Bare Metal"],"github":"https://github.com/esixtosr/12U-Bare-Metal-Homelab","external":null,"cta":null,"featured":null},"html":"<p>A compact 12U bare-metal homelab built to support network segmentation, virtualization, infrastructure services, and hands-on system administration.</p>\n<p>The rack combines physical server hardware, UniFi networking, managed switching, VLAN planning, and documentation-focused topology work for cybersecurity, networking, and self-hosted service projects.</p>"}},{"node":{"frontmatter":{"title":"CryptoChat","cover":{"publicURL":"/static/4454aeb077ddd06f059b4e572ae35bb5/01-cryptochat-main-verified-chat.png"},"gif":null,"gallery":[{"publicURL":"/static/d962687ee5a77353110d8feffc123942/02-cryptochat-fingerprint-verification.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/d5b685ef73c31e47199aa9ebd8d32ad0/03-cryptochat-architecture.svg"},{"publicURL":"/static/ed273a693c0bf99d1fadcb294b6e34ab/04-cryptochat-wireshark-encrypted-traffic.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/12600d9054a53dc6b7c2077318762a84/05-cryptochat-collapsed-sidebar.png"},{"publicURL":"/static/e7248fb5cd0bd7b60535d6432686a3ac/06-cryptochat-disconnected-state.png"}],"tech":["Python","Cryptography","X25519","AES-GCM","TCP","Wireshark"],"github":"https://github.com/esixtosr/CryptoChat","external":null,"cta":null,"featured":null},"html":"<p>CryptoChat is an encrypted peer-to-peer messaging project built to explore practical secure communication concepts, including key exchange, authenticated encryption, and fingerprint verification.</p>\n<p>The project shows how two peers establish a shared secret, derive encryption keys, verify identities, and exchange encrypted messages over TCP, with packet-level validation in Wireshark.</p>"}}]}}}